WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.726
Par for this level of
Kettle is 100 frames.

00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:08.585
Under the rules its makers
meant, the fastest run takes 186.

00:00:08.635 --> 00:00:11.140
A search found one that takes 70.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:15.498
Here Kettle closes on the wall,
slowing to five pixels a frame.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:22.423
Does it stop, get pushed
back, or go through?

00:00:22.473 --> 00:00:23.315
Through.

00:00:23.365 --> 00:00:32.119
A five-pixel move puts Kettle's front edge more than halfway into the
8-pixel wall, and the game pushes it out of the nearer side, the far one.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:36.633
Walking speed is one and a half pixels
a frame. So how did it get to five?

00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:43.951
In Frame Perfect you write the search that found
this run, then read the game's code to see how.
